# Build-time values for production builds — `expo export -p web` (Cloudflare
# Workers Builds) and EAS release builds. Committed on purpose, which is why
# .gitignore carries an exception for this one file.
#
# Only ever put publishable values here. Everything in this file is inlined into
# the JavaScript bundle that every visitor downloads, so "is it in the repo" and
# "is it secret" are two separate questions and this file only answers the first.
# Anything genuinely secret belongs in `.dev.vars` or `wrangler secret put` — see
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY, which is the server half of the pair below and is in neither
# this file nor the repo.
#
# Precedence: a real environment variable beats this file. So a Workers Builds
# build variable or an `env` entry in eas.json still wins, and this is the
# fallback that keeps a fresh clone or a fresh CI runner from silently building
# an app with no accounts in it.
#
# When a production Clerk instance replaces this development one, change the key
# here rather than only in the dashboard — otherwise the pk_test_ value below
# stays the fallback and a build that loses its env var quietly points at dev.

# Publishable by design: ships in the client bundle, names the Clerk instance
# (kind-redfish-41.clerk.accounts.dev), and authorises nothing on its own.
EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_a2luZC1yZWRmaXNoLTQxLmNsZXJrLmFjY291bnRzLmRldiQ

# The Worker that serves the API. Without an origin the app requests a bare
# `/api/...`, which works on web and silently fails in a native build.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://marquee.rocks
